      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done — the checker now prints the request pointer whenever it reports missing artifacts, to stderr, so it\u0027s visible straight from a failed CI log and a local bazel run. It only appears on a genuine miss (exit 1), not on infra errors (exit 2).\n\nI verified it against the real production lock by temporarily injecting one bogus coordinate (then reverting):\n\n```\n404   com.example.doesnotexist:fake:jar       https://gerrit-maven.storage.googleapis.com/com/example/doesnotexist/fake/1.0/fake-1.0.jar\nchecked\u003d299 mirrored\u003d298 missing\u003d1 errors\u003d0\n1 artifact(s) are not on the gerrit-maven mirror. Contributors cannot upload directly; request that the coordinates listed above be added to the mirror (see Documentation/dev-processes.txt, \"Upgrading Libraries\"):\n  https://issues.gerritcodereview.com/issues/new?component\u003d1371020\u0026template\u003d1834212\n```\n\nAll 298 real dependencies resolve; only the injected fake is flagged, exit 1. The pointer carries the direct issue-tracker link (the same Hosting \u003e googlesource component from \"Upgrading Libraries\"), so a contributor can act without leaving the build output. Added a test that the failed case includes the pointer (and that a fully-mirrored run doesn\u0027t).",
      "parentUuid": "f8109e88_e2782726",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 657,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 661,
